cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the paper and the software release."
title: "Deep Research: Bounded Returns to Orchestration"
authors:
  - family-names: "McCann Strain"
    given-names: "Peter"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Peter-McCann-Strain/bounded-returns-deep-research"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-31"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.21118281"
    description: "Archived release and paper"
abstract: >-
  Research codebase for a controlled comparison of eleven automated deep-research
  orchestration architectures, held constant on model and tools so that
  architecture is the variable. Ships 18 pattern implementations in total: the
  eleven compared in the paper plus seven later probes and controls. Ships the pattern implementations, retrieval and
  judging tools, the evaluation harness with a nine-dimension rubric and
  multi-model judge panel, experiment runners, the statistical analysis that
  produces the paper's reported numbers, and the tidy evaluation frames those
  analyses read.
keywords:
  - deep research
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - agent orchestration
  - reproducibility
  - LLM-as-judge
  - evaluation
